1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:02,833
Still, there really is someone I like.

2
00:00:02,953 --> 00:00:05,286
Is it... Takeuchi?

3
00:00:05,633 --> 00:00:08,300
Don't you have anyone you like, Suzuki?

4
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:10,333
No.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,633
I see...

6
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:21,567
I'm going to support Serizawa's love life.

7
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:28,267
Suzuki, does this go here?

8
00:00:28,367 --> 00:00:29,500
Yeah.

9
00:00:29,967 --> 00:00:31,233
Ah, sorry, Suzuki.

10
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:33,300
Looks like we're almost out of red paint.

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,643
Got it. I'll go grab some later.

12
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:38,000
Hey, Suzuki, look! Doesn't it look great?

13
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,333
- Looks awesome!
- Right?

14
00:00:39,433 --> 00:00:41,467
What do you think about
adding some flowers here?

15
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:43,133
- Around here works too.
- True.

16
00:00:43,233 --> 00:00:44,409
There's still space over here.

17
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:46,776
- Wouldn't that look great?
- Ah, let's add them later, then.

18
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,167
Suzuki looks super busy.

19
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:55,000
He barely has any time for us lately.

20
00:00:56,167 --> 00:01:00,533
Still, I never thought Suzuki would
volunteer for the festival committee.

21
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:05,400
Oh, everyone's working hard!

22
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:08,033
So cute!

23
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:09,367
Look at this.

24
00:01:09,467 --> 00:01:10,300
Whoa, amazing!

25
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:11,067
Look, look!

26
00:01:11,153 --> 00:01:12,953
I'm not talking about you.

27
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:14,267
Did Takeuchi make this?

28
00:01:14,367 --> 00:01:15,033
Yes.

29
00:01:15,133 --> 00:01:16,667
He did such an incredible job.

30
00:01:17,300 --> 00:01:18,767
That's our Takeuchi.

31
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:20,687
He's practically a master artist.

32
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:23,400
Thank you, Teacher.

33
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,767
Suzuki, where's the tape?

34
00:01:26,167 --> 00:01:27,300
Ah...

35
00:01:28,133 --> 00:01:29,200
Um...

36
00:01:32,433 --> 00:01:33,633
Suzuki!

37
00:01:33,733 --> 00:01:34,933
Here you go.

38
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,400
Oh, thanks.

39
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:38,967
Are you okay?

40
00:01:39,067 --> 00:01:41,433
Haven't you been pushing
yourself too hard lately?

41
00:01:41,867 --> 00:01:44,633
You haven't had time
to write your novel either.

42
00:01:45,567 --> 00:01:46,700
Well...

43
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,333
Sorry, I've just been a bit busy.

44
00:01:49,733 --> 00:01:51,093
Is there anything I can help with?

45
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:53,413
- If something's on your mind, you can always—
- I'm fine.

46
00:01:53,567 --> 00:01:55,167
I'm really okay.

47
00:01:55,433 --> 00:01:58,467
Ah, go help Takeuchi instead.

48
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,267
Go on.

49
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:05,900
Suzuki!

50
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,133
Ah...

51
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:11,767
What's going on with you and Suzuki?

52
00:02:14,833 --> 00:02:16,067
Huh?

53
00:02:16,167 --> 00:02:18,067
Suzuki said he doesn't
have anyone he likes?

54
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:19,633
Yeah, basically...

55
00:02:20,567 --> 00:02:22,400
So in other words...

56
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,033
You got rejected.

57
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:25,633
I didn't get rejected!

58
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:28,933
I was a little bummed
when I heard it, sure.

59
00:02:30,267 --> 00:02:33,733
But thinking about it,
there's no reason to be down.

60
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:34,633
Yeah?

61
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:37,767
Even if he doesn't like me right now...

62
00:02:37,867 --> 00:02:39,967
he might fall for me later on, right?

63
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:40,900
Right?

64
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:47,233
Besides, having no crush
means I have no rivals.

65
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,467
Isn't that super promising?

66
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:52,867
Classic Serizawa.

67
00:02:52,967 --> 00:02:55,133
The ultimate optimist, as always.

68
00:02:56,033 --> 00:02:58,933
- Terrifying.
- A total monster.

69
00:02:59,367 --> 00:03:03,333
Still, the issue is with Suzuki...

70
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,967
Don't you have one, Suzuki?

71
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:11,600
Someone you like?

72
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:14,667
No.

73
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:18,300
I see...

74
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:24,700
Ever since that day, I haven't
been able to write a single word.

75
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:25,800
No, this won't do.

76
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:29,300
I can't go on like this.
I already decided to support him.

77
00:03:30,067 --> 00:03:33,367
For now, I just need to
focus on festival prep.

78
00:03:36,367 --> 00:03:40,400
I just can't let go of
my feelings for Serizawa.

79
00:04:26,467 --> 00:04:29,333
Popular Serizawa Acts Weird Around Me.

80
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:31,200
(Traditional Festival Stall)

81
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,533
(Episode 9)
All right!

82
00:04:33,633 --> 00:04:35,600
The day is finally here.

83
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:36,933
Yeah.

84
00:04:37,433 --> 00:04:39,667
Whoa, not bad!

85
00:04:40,567 --> 00:04:42,167
Looks great.

86
00:04:43,567 --> 00:04:46,433
Still, Suzuki, you really worked hard.

87
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:48,213
The prep must have been exhausting, right?

88
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:49,700
Yes.

89
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:52,333
Though... I'd rather stay busy.

90
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:53,967
What was that?

91
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:55,933
Oh, it's nothing...

92
00:04:56,033 --> 00:04:58,400
It was all thanks to everyone's help.

93
00:05:29,733 --> 00:05:30,933
Suzuki.

94
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,600
Well?

95
00:05:33,667 --> 00:05:34,933
How do I look?

96
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,500
Yeah.

97
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:39,567
It suits you so well.

98
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,900
Did your heart skip a beat?

99
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:47,267
- N-No, it didn't.
- Come on, you're supposed to say yes!

100
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,600
All right, lead the way, Captain!

101
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:50,500
Huh?

102
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,233
Okay! Everyone, bring it in!

103
00:05:52,333 --> 00:05:53,367
Yeah!

104
00:05:53,467 --> 00:05:55,067
That's the spirit!

105
00:05:58,367 --> 00:06:02,367
Let's hear a few words from Suzuki!

106
00:06:05,033 --> 00:06:08,800
Um... thank you so much, everyone.

107
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:13,367
You helped me out so much during prep.

108
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:17,300
Let's do our best today, too!

109
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:21,533
All right! Let's get fired up!

110
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,500
One, two, three, fight!

111
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:29,733
Welcome!

112
00:06:31,233 --> 00:06:32,600
Here you go.

113
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:40,500
Nice, nice!

114
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,933
(Soothing Turtle Stand)

115
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:46,747
- This little turtle is cute just like you.
- It really is adorable.

116
00:06:51,833 --> 00:06:54,433
(Free Weightlifting)

117
00:06:54,967 --> 00:06:56,267
Welcome!

118
00:06:56,367 --> 00:06:57,800
Want to try yo-yo balloon fishing?

119
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:01,767
Excuse me, do you know where Kou-chan is?

120
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:02,533
Kou-chan?

121
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:04,233
I heard he was here.

122
00:07:04,333 --> 00:07:06,043
- Do you know where Kou-chan is?
- Kou-chan?

123
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:08,833
He has pale skin and black hair.

124
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,367
Black hair, huh...

125
00:07:10,467 --> 00:07:11,543
Do you know where Kou-chan is?

126
00:07:11,567 --> 00:07:12,367
Wait, Kou-chan?

127
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:13,567
Yeah.

128
00:07:14,167 --> 00:07:15,300
Kou-chan!

129
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,600
Huh?

130
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:18,067
It's Kou-chan!

131
00:07:18,833 --> 00:07:19,733
No, I'm not.

132
00:07:19,833 --> 00:07:20,833
- Huh?
- What?

133
00:07:20,900 --> 00:07:21,900
- Huh?
- What?

134
00:07:22,033 --> 00:07:23,200
Aren't you Kou-chan?

135
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,067
N-No, I'm not.

136
00:07:25,167 --> 00:07:26,467
Then what's your name?

137
00:07:28,867 --> 00:07:30,467
Suzuki Hajime.

138
00:07:30,567 --> 00:07:31,847
- Suzuki Hajime?
- Suzuki Hajime.

139
00:07:31,933 --> 00:07:33,367
- Yeah, I'm Suzuki.
- What?!

140
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:35,767
You look just like Kou-chan!

141
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,967
Huh? You're really not him?

142
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:40,933
- His name's Hajime-chan.
- Hajime-chan?

143
00:07:41,267 --> 00:07:43,433
Oh, so you're Hajime-chan!

144
00:07:43,533 --> 00:07:45,633
Where on earth did Kou-chan go?

145
00:07:45,733 --> 00:07:48,400
- This toy is actually pretty fun.
- Better than I expected!

146
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:48,933
Huh?

147
00:07:49,033 --> 00:07:50,867
It's so lively over here!

148
00:07:50,967 --> 00:07:52,533
Wait...

149
00:07:52,633 --> 00:07:53,667
Isn't that Suzuki?

150
00:07:53,767 --> 00:07:54,967
Incredible!

151
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:01,133
We completely sold out!

152
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:04,233
All right! That wraps it up for us too.

153
00:08:05,967 --> 00:08:07,300
- Sold out!
- Sweet!

154
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,367
That's awesome! Way to go!

155
00:08:09,467 --> 00:08:11,833
(Sold Out. Thank you for your support!)

156
00:08:13,267 --> 00:08:14,633
Everyone...

157
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,600
Thank you for all your hard work.

158
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:19,676
Everything's taken care of here.

159
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:20,940
You're all free to look around.

160
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,933
- Seriously?
- Awesome!

161
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,609
- Koharu, let's go check it out.
- Sure thing!

162
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:26,633
- Takeuchi, let's grab some food.
- Sounds good.

163
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:34,100
Serizawa, why don't you go with Takeuchi?

164
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:36,433
Nah, I'm good.

165
00:08:36,900 --> 00:08:40,100
But it's the festival...

166
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:40,933
Why?

167
00:08:41,033 --> 00:08:42,667
Didn't you say we have free time?

168
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:48,800
Then I want to hang out with you, Suzuki.

169
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,367
Don't say things like that...

170
00:08:54,433 --> 00:08:55,700
Huh?

171
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:57,333
Ah, sorry.

172
00:08:57,433 --> 00:09:00,300
Oh, I still have rounds to
do as a committee member.

173
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:01,433
I have to get going.

174
00:09:01,533 --> 00:09:04,500
So I can't stay with you, Serizawa.

175
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,900
Sorry.

176
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,933
Hey...

177
00:09:17,967 --> 00:09:20,800
I really do want to be with Serizawa.

178
00:09:21,467 --> 00:09:23,433
But if we stay together like this...

179
00:09:23,933 --> 00:09:26,400
I'll never be able to move
on from these feelings.

180
00:09:26,667 --> 00:09:28,733
That Suzuki guy is seriously obnoxious.

181
00:09:28,833 --> 00:09:30,667
He used to be a total loner.

182
00:09:30,767 --> 00:09:32,487
Now he suddenly acts like he's Mr. Popular.

183
00:09:32,533 --> 00:09:34,509
He even joined the committee.
Who does he think he is?

184
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:37,767
Come to think of it,
Serizawa's pretty ridiculous too.

185
00:09:37,867 --> 00:09:41,367
Whenever it involves Suzuki,
he gets all fired up.

186
00:09:41,467 --> 00:09:43,600
He even claimed he likes BL now.

187
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,800
Right?

188
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,167
What's Serizawa's deal anyway?

189
00:09:46,267 --> 00:09:49,700
Don't tell me he actually
has a crush on Suzuki?

190
00:09:50,367 --> 00:09:52,667
- Gross.
- No way, that's disgusting.

191
00:09:52,767 --> 00:09:54,100
You're wrong.

192
00:09:54,367 --> 00:09:55,167
Suzuki?

193
00:09:55,267 --> 00:09:58,633
Serizawa does not like me.

194
00:10:01,667 --> 00:10:02,900
Huh?

195
00:10:03,567 --> 00:10:09,033
And there's nothing
weird or gross about him!

196
00:10:09,133 --> 00:10:13,867
He's the coolest and
kindest person in the world.

197
00:10:13,967 --> 00:10:15,700
He brings sunshine to everyone.

198
00:10:16,233 --> 00:10:20,367
- And besides...
- What are you even babbling about?

199
00:10:20,467 --> 00:10:24,100
We were just messing around.

200
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,600
Right?

201
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:26,700
Yeah.

202
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:29,367
Like Serizawa would ever like Suzuki.

203
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,433
That's completely impossible.

204
00:10:32,133 --> 00:10:33,533
Are you guys done yet?

205
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,667
Matsuno?

206
00:10:40,100 --> 00:10:41,433
Cut it out.

207
00:10:42,833 --> 00:10:45,467
You're just jealous of Suzuki.

208
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,600
What?

209
00:10:46,700 --> 00:10:48,533
- What are you talking about?
- Just admit it.

210
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,800
You're envious, aren't you?

211
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:55,767
Envious that Suzuki gets to be friends
with the popular kids.

212
00:10:56,667 --> 00:10:57,733
Hey, wait a second.

213
00:10:57,833 --> 00:10:59,967
Why are you sticking up for Suzuki?

214
00:11:02,167 --> 00:11:04,400
Because...

215
00:11:08,633 --> 00:11:10,267
I just...

216
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,400
I want to keep being friends with Suzuki.

217
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:30,800
About earlier... thank you.

218
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:38,100
And also...

219
00:11:40,467 --> 00:11:41,767
I'm sorry.

220
00:11:45,067 --> 00:11:49,633
About what happened back in freshman year.

221
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,233
I've always wanted to apologize to you.

222
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:59,433
Back then, I was only
thinking about myself.

223
00:11:59,533 --> 00:12:00,567
No way.

224
00:12:00,667 --> 00:12:01,767
Gross.

225
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:05,900
Disgusting.

226
00:12:07,567 --> 00:12:09,267
Saying awful things like that...

227
00:12:11,167 --> 00:12:12,967
and hurting you like that, Suzuki.

228
00:12:17,433 --> 00:12:18,967
I'm truly sorry.

229
00:12:26,133 --> 00:12:29,667
(Romeo and Romeo)
(Class 2-2 Theater / Drama Club)

230
00:12:30,367 --> 00:12:32,100
Romeo is so handsome.

231
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,300
He's all right.

232
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,667
Oh, Serizawa.

233
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:35,800
Huh?

234
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,100
Aren't you with Suzuki?

235
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:38,300
Ah, yeah.

236
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:39,867
He seemed pretty busy.

237
00:12:42,367 --> 00:12:44,267
Dude, you bought way too much stuff.

238
00:12:44,367 --> 00:12:45,233
What did you get?

239
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:47,053
This is ridiculous. How much did you spend?

240
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,167
What's going on?

241
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:49,433
Look at all this.

242
00:12:49,533 --> 00:12:50,700
Ooh, the good stuff!

243
00:12:51,933 --> 00:12:53,233
Hands off!

244
00:12:53,333 --> 00:12:55,533
Hey, did you guys hear?

245
00:12:55,633 --> 00:12:57,376
Teacher Usami's girlfriend
is at the gym right now!

246
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,967
Apparently an event is starting soon.

247
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:00,667
- Really?
- Let's all go check it out!

248
00:13:01,433 --> 00:13:03,333
- Let's go.
- Come on!

249
00:13:05,033 --> 00:13:10,633
To be honest, I've always
admired you, Suzuki.

250
00:13:11,267 --> 00:13:11,900
Huh...?

251
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,233
The truth is, I have
an idol I really like too.

252
00:13:19,533 --> 00:13:20,733
An idol?

253
00:13:27,367 --> 00:13:29,400
(Oky)
This guy right here.

254
00:13:30,067 --> 00:13:31,933
I never told my friends.

255
00:13:33,833 --> 00:13:36,533
Because I was afraid if I did...

256
00:13:37,033 --> 00:13:39,767
they'd reject me or laugh at me.

257
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:46,067
Seeing you stay true to what you love...

258
00:13:46,167 --> 00:13:49,967
even when you were all on your own...

259
00:13:50,067 --> 00:13:52,000
I thought that was truly incredible.

260
00:13:54,667 --> 00:14:00,867
Not really. I'm not that confident either.

261
00:14:01,900 --> 00:14:05,000
Besides, there's nothing
wrong with keeping it to yourself.

262
00:14:06,633 --> 00:14:13,200
Share it if you want,
keep it private if you don't.

263
00:14:13,767 --> 00:14:17,800
No matter how you choose
to support your idol, Matsuno...

264
00:14:18,667 --> 00:14:24,133
those feelings belong entirely to you.

265
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:33,500
You really are amazing, Suzuki.

266
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:39,467
And Serizawa too.

267
00:14:39,567 --> 00:14:40,767
Huh?

268
00:14:44,400 --> 00:14:45,833
Um...

269
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:57,633
This is Suzuki's.
Could you give it back to him for me?

270
00:14:57,733 --> 00:14:59,067
I refuse.

271
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,867
Huh?

272
00:15:00,967 --> 00:15:03,000
No way. I really won't.

273
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,500
Absolutely not.

274
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:06,200
I totally refuse.

275
00:15:06,933 --> 00:15:10,139
Why do you have to be so against it?

276
00:15:10,233 --> 00:15:14,500
Because if I'm the one who returns it...

277
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:17,867
he'll think it means
you're cutting ties with him.

278
00:15:18,733 --> 00:15:22,567
"Does Matsuno not want
to talk to me anymore?"

279
00:15:22,667 --> 00:15:26,267
"Are we never going to be friends again?"

280
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:30,900
If Suzuki thinks that, he'll get hurt.

281
00:15:32,367 --> 00:15:33,967
I don't want that.

282
00:15:35,300 --> 00:15:38,600
I never want Suzuki to get hurt.

283
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:40,800
Not even for a single second.

284
00:15:47,633 --> 00:15:50,133
I genuinely think he's remarkable.

285
00:15:51,733 --> 00:15:54,500
Serizawa is such a great guy.

286
00:15:55,567 --> 00:15:58,700
I had no idea Serizawa did that for me...

287
00:16:00,233 --> 00:16:04,433
Thanks for hearing me out.

288
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,967
From now on, I'll keep
supporting my idol...

289
00:16:09,067 --> 00:16:10,767
just the way I want to.

290
00:16:11,033 --> 00:16:13,333
Yeah, I think that's great.

291
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:26,300
So make sure you cherish
what you love too, Suzuki.

292
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:29,400
The things that matter to you.

293
00:16:44,733 --> 00:16:47,700
The things I love...

294
00:16:50,267 --> 00:16:51,533
Suzuki!

295
00:16:56,500 --> 00:16:59,033
All done packing up?

296
00:17:00,933 --> 00:17:02,800
Ah... yeah.

297
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:05,167
All right, come with me for a second.

298
00:17:05,267 --> 00:17:06,400
Huh?

299
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:09,800
Here we go.

300
00:17:09,900 --> 00:17:11,200
Ready, set...

301
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,100
Ah!

302
00:17:12,200 --> 00:17:15,500
Suzuki! Great job today...

303
00:17:17,467 --> 00:17:18,467
Whoa, we startled him!

304
00:17:18,533 --> 00:17:20,800
You were so busy on the committee...

305
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:23,233
did you even have time
to visit other classes?

306
00:17:23,333 --> 00:17:28,267
Serizawa said we should throw
an appreciation party for you.

307
00:17:28,367 --> 00:17:33,100
Apparently he bought snacks
from the whole school by himself.

308
00:17:35,733 --> 00:17:37,867
Well? Did your heart skip a beat?

309
00:17:41,967 --> 00:17:43,433
It did.

310
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:55,300
Didn't expect it to double
as Takeuchi's heartbreak party too.

311
00:17:55,400 --> 00:17:55,967
Heartbreak?

312
00:17:56,067 --> 00:17:58,133
- Way to read the room!
- It's fine.

313
00:17:58,233 --> 00:17:59,667
It's all right.

314
00:17:59,767 --> 00:18:01,567
I knew it from the start anyway.

315
00:18:01,833 --> 00:18:05,500
After all, I fell for a teacher
who could never love me back.

316
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:07,133
A... a teacher?

317
00:18:07,233 --> 00:18:10,333
Oh, didn't I tell you, Suzuki?

318
00:18:10,933 --> 00:18:18,133
I had a crush on Teacher Usami.

319
00:18:18,767 --> 00:18:20,400
Teacher Usami?

320
00:18:21,367 --> 00:18:22,667
Yeah.

321
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:28,400
Except today, on stage in the gym...

322
00:18:29,133 --> 00:18:31,433
Teacher Usami proposed publicly.

323
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:35,600
Congratulations!

324
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,633
Go get her, Teacher!

325
00:18:37,733 --> 00:18:39,767
(High Schoolers' Honest Thoughts)

326
00:18:40,967 --> 00:18:42,533
Go for it, Teacher!

327
00:18:43,533 --> 00:18:46,200
- So romantic!
- You got this!

328
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,333
I love you.

329
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:53,500
More than anyone else in the world.

330
00:18:59,167 --> 00:19:00,767
Oh my gosh, oh my gosh!

331
00:19:01,567 --> 00:19:03,833
For the rest of our lives...

332
00:19:03,933 --> 00:19:06,333
will you marry me and
be my partner forever?

333
00:19:09,767 --> 00:19:11,133
Yes.

334
00:19:14,733 --> 00:19:16,467
Congratulations to you both!

335
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:18,633
Congratulations, Teacher!

336
00:19:29,567 --> 00:19:31,467
It hurts so much...

337
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:34,400
There, there, Takeuchi.

338
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:36,933
Want some takoyaki?

339
00:19:38,467 --> 00:19:43,633
Or do you want a hug from me?

340
00:19:43,733 --> 00:19:44,967
No.

341
00:19:45,867 --> 00:19:47,500
Don't be nice to me right now.

342
00:19:48,933 --> 00:19:50,667
I might end up falling for you.

343
00:19:54,600 --> 00:19:56,333
I wouldn't mind if you did.

344
00:19:59,067 --> 00:20:00,067
Huh?

345
00:20:05,800 --> 00:20:08,800
Without your glasses,
you're actually pretty cute.

346
00:20:11,167 --> 00:20:12,300
What?

347
00:20:18,133 --> 00:20:20,000
Hey, let me see again!

348
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:20,967
See?

349
00:20:21,067 --> 00:20:23,133
Wait, is another BL romance starting here?

350
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,933
Takeuchi...

351
00:20:27,700 --> 00:20:30,167
Wait, so everyone knew about this?

352
00:20:30,267 --> 00:20:31,567
Serizawa knew too?

353
00:20:31,667 --> 00:20:34,033
- Yeah.
- What?

354
00:20:34,633 --> 00:20:35,967
Huh?

355
00:20:36,267 --> 00:20:37,767
Then...

356
00:20:39,067 --> 00:20:41,233
What is Serizawa going to do?

357
00:20:41,867 --> 00:20:42,867
Me?

358
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:44,600
What do you mean?

359
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,067
Wait...

360
00:20:46,667 --> 00:20:48,000
What is going on?

361
00:20:48,100 --> 00:20:51,400
Takeuchi wasn't the one Serizawa liked?

362
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:54,267
Then who on earth is it?

363
00:20:57,167 --> 00:20:58,900
Forget about that for now. Just eat!

364
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:01,600
We got all this special food for Suzuki.

365
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:04,900
Which one do you want?

366
00:21:06,933 --> 00:21:08,700
Whatever...

367
00:21:09,133 --> 00:21:10,333
I'll stop overthinking.

368
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:27,000
By the way, did you
talk with Matsuno today?

369
00:21:27,967 --> 00:21:29,033
Yeah.

370
00:21:29,133 --> 00:21:30,400
Thanks to you, Serizawa.

371
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:32,167
We talked.

372
00:21:33,967 --> 00:21:37,067
Does that mean he'll become...

373
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,400
your best friend again?

374
00:21:40,533 --> 00:21:41,833
Huh?

375
00:21:43,367 --> 00:21:45,300
Didn't you say before?

376
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:47,900
That you two used to be closest.

377
00:21:49,933 --> 00:21:51,633
Oh...

378
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:56,933
Still, he won't be number one.

379
00:21:59,133 --> 00:22:01,067
Because I have...

380
00:22:03,233 --> 00:22:04,833
I have Serizawa.

381
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:10,567
Even if... no matter
who Serizawa likes...

382
00:22:14,133 --> 00:22:16,733
Wait, that hurts, Serizawa!

383
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:20,033
I was just so happy...

384
00:22:20,133 --> 00:22:23,833
to hear you say that!

385
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:29,467
And I've always wanted
to hug you like this, Suzuki.

386
00:22:32,033 --> 00:22:33,967
Me too...

387
00:22:34,400 --> 00:22:38,133
I like Serizawa.

388
00:22:38,233 --> 00:22:39,467
Hm?

389
00:22:40,367 --> 00:22:41,867
What did you just say?

390
00:22:42,333 --> 00:22:43,933
It's a secret.

391
00:22:44,033 --> 00:22:48,033
Because these feelings are my own treasure.

392
00:22:48,133 --> 00:22:50,167
Aw, come on!

393
00:22:50,267 --> 00:22:51,433
Tell me!

394
00:22:51,533 --> 00:22:52,667
No way.

395
00:22:52,767 --> 00:22:55,067
- Stop teasing me!
- Whoa, close one!

396
00:22:55,167 --> 00:22:56,533
How about some of this?

397
00:22:56,633 --> 00:22:57,633
What if I eat this?

398
00:22:57,667 --> 00:22:58,943
If I eat this, I don't
have to tell you, right?

399
00:22:58,967 --> 00:22:59,733
Deal.

400
00:22:59,833 --> 00:23:01,393
(Next Episode Preview)
(BL Novel Finale)

401
00:23:01,967 --> 00:23:03,533
I finished writing it.

402
00:23:03,633 --> 00:23:04,300
- I want to read it!
- Me too!

403
00:23:04,400 --> 00:23:05,400
Sorry.

404
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:07,133
I'll let everyone read it later.

405
00:23:07,233 --> 00:23:09,467
I kind of feel like crying right now.

406
00:23:09,567 --> 00:23:10,667
Ah, sorry.

407
00:23:12,433 --> 00:23:14,700
(This program is entirely fictional.)
